## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to model task dependencies as a DAG and compute an optimal parallel schedule using topological ordering and dynamic programming.

## Key Concepts

- **Topological sort**: Ordering nodes such that all prerequisites come before dependent tasks
- **DAG DP**: Computing the longest path in a directed acyclic graph
- **Cycle detection**: Using indegree counts to identify cycles (if not all nodes are processed)
- **Time complexity**: O(n + m) where n is nodes and m is edges

## Code Example

```javascript
function earliestFinish(n, edges, duration) {
  const adj = Array.from({ length: n }, () => []);
  const indeg = Array(n).fill(0);

  for (const [u, v] of edges) {
    adj[u].push(v);
    indeg[v]++;
  }

  const finish = duration.slice();
  const q = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    if (indeg[i] === 0) q.push(i);
  }

  let processed = 0;

  while (q.length) {
    const u = q.shift();
    processed++;

    for (const v of adj[u]) {
      finish[v] = Math.max(finish[v], finish[u] + duration[v]);
      indeg[v]--;
      if (indeg[v] === 0) q.push(v);
    }
  }

  if (processed !== n) return -1;
  return Math.max(...finish);
}
```

## Key Takeaways

- Unlimited workers means tasks run in parallel when dependencies allow
- The finish time of a task is the maximum of (prerequisite finish + its own duration)
- The pipeline completes when the slowest path (critical path) finishes

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to blend BFS intuition with shortest-path techniques under a hop constraint and to reconstruct a path from augmented state.

## Key Concepts
- Augmented state graph: (node, hops)
- Dijkstra with 2D dist and predecessor tracking
- Path reconstruction from (node, hops) chain
- Time/space: O((N*H + M*H) log(N*H))

## Code Example

```javascript
function shortestPathWithHops(graph, S, T, H) {
  // graph: {u: [{to,w}, ...], ...}
  const dist = new Map();
  const prev = new Map();
  // min-heap assumed available: push({time, node, hops})
  const heap = new MinHeap((a,b)=>a.time-b.time);
  dist.set(`${S}|0`, 0);
  heap.push({time:0, node:S, hops:0});
  while (!heap.isEmpty()) {
    const {time,u,k} = heap.pop();
    if (time !== dist.get(`${u}|${k}`)) continue;
    for (const {to:v, w} of (graph[u] || [])) {
      const nk = k + 1;
      if (nk > H) continue;
      const nd = time + w;
      const key = `${v}|${nk}`;
      if (nd < (dist.get(key) ?? Infinity)) {
        dist.set(key, nd);
        prev.set(key, `${u}|${k}`);
        heap.push({time: nd, node: v, hops: nk});
      }
    }
  }
  let bestTime = Infinity; let bestKey = null;
  for (let k = 0; k <= H; k++) {
    const key = `${T}|${k}`;
    const d = dist.get(key);
    if (d != null && d < bestTime) { bestTime = d; bestKey = key; }
  }
  const path = [];
  if (bestKey) {
    let cur = bestKey;
    while (cur) {
      const [node] = cur.split('|');
      path.push(node);
      cur = prev.get(cur);
    }
    path.reverse();
  }
  return { time: bestTime, path };
}
```

